{
	"//": "Type hubs carrying a #list anchor, mapped to the plural the hub's own heading uses. Module:Entity/Navplates matches a type string against the keys by singular and plural, and says \"More <value>\". `overrides` covers the cases pluralisation cannot reach. `roles` is a separate, exact-match map from a vehicle's Role to its hub: role values are generic words (Medical, Mining, Cargo), so matching them against the shared `hubs` keyspace would let an item hub of the same name capture them. Each entry names the vehicle family its hub lists, because most of these hubs are spacecraft: a ground vehicle's Medical role must not link Medical ships, which does not list it. `kinds` is an exact-match map from a resolved entity kind to the one hub all its pages browse to; a kind listed there skips every type lookup, because its type strings are a different vocabulary (commodity substances) that collides with item hubs (Food). `selects` names the Bucket selector a hub's own #list grid uses, and a hub listed there is counted by it instead of by Subject type.",
